# Reverse proxy in front of Asano. Nothing here needs editing — set
# SITE_ADDRESS in .env instead.
#
# Unset (the default): listens on :80, plain HTTP, no domain — works
# immediately for a local eval with nothing to configure, and Caddy makes no
# attempt at HTTPS since there's no real hostname to request a certificate
# for.
#
# Set to a real domain (SITE_ADDRESS=your-domain.com in .env, DNS already
# pointed at this server, 80/443 open): Caddy requests and renews a real
# Let's Encrypt certificate for it automatically. Nothing else changes.
{$SITE_ADDRESS::80} {
	reverse_proxy asano:3000
}
